{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== HANDOFF #14 — e369 + parity epic 3e73. READ THIS, THEN #13, THEN #12. ===\n\nWORKTREE /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-jira-family. ALWAYS: export PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\"\nSpare worktree /Users/joeoakhart/agent-5200-diag is kept parked on origin/main for CLOSES.\nDO NOT trust the board below — read the tickets.\n\n*** ONE THING BLOCKS EVERYTHING. FIX IT FIRST. ***\n[rebar:e47e-a33d-b9cf-4421] — the GATING `pip-audit` job fails on `click 8.2.1` /\n**PYSEC-2026-2132** (fixed in click 8.3.3), pinned in the committed `uv.lock` (~line 711). This is a\nPRE-EXISTING property of `main`, reproducing on every change pushed today at head sha 4214516f95 —\nat least six of them. **IT IS NOT RECHECKABLE**: the workflow retries only DB-UNREACHABLE failures,\nand the log shows the audit succeeded on attempt 1/3, i.e. it reached the advisory DB and found a\nreal finding. Posting `recheck` will never clear it. FIVE FINISHED CHANGES ARE QUEUED BEHIND IT.\nWHAT I ESTABLISHED (do not redo): click is TRANSITIVE (no `import click` anywhere in src); the\nvulnerable `click.edit()` is used NOWHERE in src/tests/scripts; `requires-python` is >=3.11 while\nclick 8.3.3 needs only >=3.10; nothing pins click below 8.3 outside optional `cli` extras\n(`uvicorn>=7.0`, `python-dotenv>=5.0[cli]`, `httpx==8.*[cli]`, `httpx2>=8.4[cli]`); and pyproject\nhas NO click constraint. YET `uv lock --upgrade-package click` (even with `--refresh-package`) is a\nNO-OP, leaving 8.2.1 and only an unrelated `zipfile-zstd` marker drift. LEADING HYPOTHESIS: a\nresolver-version mismatch — this host's uv is 0.7.18 (2025-07-01) while `uv.lock` was just\nregenerated by change 1219 \"ce5d: go uv-canonical with a committed lock\" (MERGED). Check the lock's\nrevision header and the uv version CI uses.\nPREFERENCE ORDER: (1) minimal `uv.lock` bump to click >= 8.3.3 — no gate weakening; (2) ONLY if\nimpossible, a narrowly-justified `--ignore-vuln PYSEC-2026-2132` with a REMOVE-WHEN comment,\nreported prominently as weakening a security gate. NEVER a wholesale dependency refresh (huge risky\ndiff, destabilises in-flight changes). An agent owns this; ONLY ONE agent may touch `uv.lock`.\n\n--- FIVE CHANGES PUSHED, ALL BLOCKED ONLY BY THE ABOVE ---\n  1231  5200  pin the inbound-update assignee mint gap        LLM-Review +1\n  1232  8d68  mint the identity on inbound updates too        LLM-Review +1\n  1233  2944  replace the tests that cannot fail              LLM-Review +1\n  1234  79d5  pin DC comment/description convergence          awaiting LLM vote\n  1235  cedc  characterize the DC backend by value            awaiting LLM vote\nFor 1234 the author confirmed EVERY validating job is green — including pytest on py3.11, the CI\nbaseline — with pip-audit the only red. Expect the same for the others. Once e47e lands, re-trigger\nand these should go straight to submittable with no rework.\n\n--- BOARD ---\ne369: 30/32 closed. OPEN: 5200 (in_progress) and 8d68 (in_progress) — both have their fix PUSHED.\n3e73: epic CERTIFIED and IN_PROGRESS at last (five review rounds). ALL FOUR P1 children CLAIMED and\n  in_progress: cedc, 79d5, 2944, bd9e. bd9e is claimed but DELIBERATELY NOT STARTED — it collides\n  with 79d5 on `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py`, so serialize it AFTER 1234 lands. P2 children\n  0fad (certified-but-stale-head) and 2127 (BLOCKED, diverged 4->2->3->3->1->3->8 findings over 8\n  rounds) are Cloud-side and MUST NOT gate DC; 2127 needs investigative rework on Cloud's retry\n  taxonomy, not another editing round — leave it.\n\n--- NEW DC DEFECT FOUND AND FIXED THIS STRETCH: 8d68 ---\n[rebar:8d68-a740-4f56-4b3a] the inbound UPDATE path never mints an assignee identity.\n`inbound_differ._diff_jira_vs_local:185-188` emits only the SCALAR `assignee` (a bare string);\nthe `assignee_identity` dict the mapper already computes at `inbound_fields:223-225` is dropped\nbecause it is not in `field_map`. So `apply_inbound_records:369` hands a STRING to\n`_ensure_inbound_assignee_identity`, which returns at `:100` on `if not isinstance(assignee, dict)`\n— silently, because it is best-effort by contract. The CREATE path at `:200-203` passes the raw dict\nand mints fine, which is why every identity the harness ever produced came from there and this\nstayed invisible. NOT a 5f48 regression: 5f48 fixed KEY SELECTION *inside* that guard, and the\nupdate path returns before the guard is reached.\n**HOW IT WAS FOUND IS THE POINT.** J11's assignee oracle was VACUOUS (it compared\n`ensure_identity_for`'s return against itself). Once repaired it reached its real assertion for the\nfirst time and immediately reported this. A test cell had been reporting green for months while\nasserting nothing.\nFIX (signed off, pushed as 1232): plumb `assignee_identity` through the differ and key the mint on\n`account_id`/`display`. **DO NOT \"fix\" it by letting the mint accept a bare string** — on DC the\nscalar is `name` (== the external id) so it looks right, but on CLOUD the scalar is the DISPLAY\nNAME, so minting on it would register every Cloud user under the wrong id: silent no-op becomes\nsilent corruption. The differ/applier are deployment-neutral, so a CLOUD-side test proving the mint\nkeys on `accountId` was required as the guard against exactly that.\n\n--- 79d5's MUTATION LEDGER CONTAINS THE EPIC'S BEST SINGLE PIECE OF EVIDENCE ---\nDropping the DC sanitizer injection left the CONVERGENCE assertion PASSING — because DC's and\nCloud's comment truncation output is BYTE-IDENTICAL (same 32767 limit, same\n`\" … [truncated by reconciler]\"` suffix, same keep-computation). Only the RECORDING check caught it.\nThat empirically confirms the review finding that a value-based discriminator there is unfalsifiable.\nThe author also improved on the plan: both suites had compared landed length against\n`WIKI_DESCRIPTION_LIMIT` — the constant under test — which is self-consistent under a raised limit,\nso a loosened limit left convergence green. Each now spells Jira's real ceiling as a LITERAL and\nroutes pass 1's output through `_as_jira_would_store()` before pass 2, so loosening the limit breaks\nCONVERGENCE ITSELF. Verified by mutation.\n\n--- TRAPS ADDED THIS STRETCH (earlier ones in #13 still hold) ---\n * `relation_snapshot.py:141` ABORTS ON ANY NON-EMPTY `git status --porcelain` IN THE SHARED TRACKER\n   — untracked files included. THIS, not lock contention, is the real cause of `store-read-failure`\n   / INDETERMINATE from rebar gate commands. Gate every review/close on a clean\n   `git -C .tickets-tracker status --porcelain`. (Found by the concurrent queue agent.)\n * `rebar review-plan --status` does NOT reliably detect a plan REWRITE — it reported only\n   `stale-head` for cc77 despite two edits after signing. Do not use it as proof a plan is unchanged.\n * A ticket's `file_impact` IS REVIEWED MATERIAL. 79d5 was blocked once purely because the\n   file_impact I declared early still named Cloud's existing files after the Approach was rewritten\n   to create new ones. The \"grep the whole document after editing\" sweep must cover file_impact too.\n * A `set-file-impact`/`comment` write CAN FAIL SILENTLY with `flock: could not acquire lock after\n   60s`. Always re-read and verify, then retry.\n * CLAIMING FOUR SIBLINGS NEEDED FOUR DIFFERENT HEAD SHAS — each certified against a different\n   commit, and the claim gate compares HEAD to the attestation's sha. Park HEAD per ticket\n   (`git checkout -q <verified-sha>`), claim, move on. The epic and 79d5 happened to share one."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785712069568659001,"uuid":"3455b0c1-12df-477c-9380-807f2ac7a948"}